  "kind": "fix",
  "title": "# AmberX recorder: opt-in mic so both sides of a session get recorded (Brett, Nov 1 ~4 AM) Read CLA…",
  "asked": "# AmberX recorder: opt-in mic so both sides of a session get recorded (Brett, Nov 1 ~4 AM) Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md, _claude/persona.md, then apps/amberx-droid, the audio-output-recorder plugin, and the reports _claude/builds/reports/rec-control.md and amberx-fix-loop-securescreen.md. Opus, one session. Git login works: plain `git push`. 0. WAIT: poll every 60 s (max 3 h) until origin/main contains the amberx-listeners build (git log origin/main --oneline | grep -i 'listener', or origin/claude/amberx-listeners is an ancestor of origin/main). Then git merge origin/main and read _claude/builds/reports/amberx-listeners.md. Build on its single-listener / mic-ownership work; don't fight it for the mic. Brett: the Audio Output Recorder records only phone playback (Claude's side). He wants his own voice too, so whole sessions are recorded. 1. Add an opt-in MIC source to the existing recorder (no new recorder): Settings toggle 'Record my mic too' (OFF by default), plus a per-session choice in the axHub recorder_start call (new optional arg `mic: true|false`, default = the setting). recorder_start stays a straight approval (confirm), and the approval text must say 'Playback + MIC' when the mic is on. 2. Capture: playback (MediaProjection AudioPlaybackCapture, as today) + mic (AudioRecord, VOICE_COMMUNICATION or VOICE_RECOGNITION source so echo cancellation helps) as TWO separate tracks per chunk (e.g. stereo L=Brett mic, R=playback, or two files with a shared timeline). Keep 30-min chunks, same naming, same upload to the session group on axHub. Two tracks lets the Chat viewer's 2-voice export and future transcription tell speakers apart. 3. Mic sharing: Android only lets one app use the mic at a time in many cases (and the Claude app's voice mode is using it during a call). Detect when the mic is unavailable or silenced by the OS (Android reports silenced capture) and record playback-only with a clear 'mic busy' marker in the chunk metadata + a notification, instead of failing. Document the limitation honestly in the report. 4. Privacy: persistent notification shows 'Recording: playback + mic'; the mic stops instantly from the notification; RECORD_AUDIO permission requested only when the toggle is first turned on; nothing records without the approved start. Note in Settings that the mic picks up anyone in the room. 5. Single owner: respect the listener fix: the recorder must not create a second listener/subscriber; mic is released when recording stops. Tests: toggle default off, approval text, two-track output, mic-busy fallback, release on stop, no second listener. Full AmberX tests + local test block from .github/workflows/android.yml + theme/controls/lifecycle checks. Android code compiles in CI; make sure the workflow builds the APK and name the artifact. Screenshots of the setting + notification (phone) to UI Review via framework/cli/shot.mjs, group 'Recorder mic - Nov 1'. Commit, fetch+merge origin/main, retest, `git push origin HEAD:main` (never force). Report at _claude/builds/reports/recorder-mic.md incl. 'install the new APK' and where to get it. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault).",
